#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:1
msgid "OBLITERATUS Analysis Modules — Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:3
msgid ""
"OBLITERATUS includes 28 analysis modules for mechanistic interpretability"
" of refusal in LLMs. These modules help understand how and where refusal "
"behaviors are encoded before performing abliteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:8
msgid "Core Analysis (Run These First)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:10
msgid "1. Alignment Imprint Detection (`alignment_imprint.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:11
msgid ""
"Fingerprints whether a model was trained via DPO, RLHF, CAI, or SFT. This"
" determines which extraction strategy will work best."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:14
msgid "2. Concept Cone Geometry (`concept_geometry.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:15
msgid ""
"Determines if refusal is a single linear direction or a polyhedral cone "
"(set of multiple mechanisms). Single-direction models respond well to "
"`basic`; polyhedral models need `advanced` or `surgical`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:19
msgid "3. Refusal Logit Lens (`logit_lens.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:20
msgid ""
"Identifies the specific layer where a model \"decides\" to refuse by "
"decoding intermediate layer representations into token space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:23
msgid "4. Ouroboros Detection (`anti_ouroboros.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:24
msgid ""
"Identifies if a model attempts to \"self-repair\" refusal behaviors after"
" excision. Reports a risk score (0-1). High scores mean additional "
"refinement passes are needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:28
msgid "5. Causal Tracing (`causal_tracing.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:29
msgid ""
"Identifies which components (layers, heads, MLPs) are causally necessary "
"for refusal behavior using activation patching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:34
msgid "Geometric Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:36
msgid "6. Cross-Layer Alignment (`cross_layer.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:37
msgid ""
"Measures how refusal directions align across different layers. High "
"alignment means the refusal signal is consistent; low alignment suggests "
"layer-specific mechanisms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:41
msgid "7. Residual Stream Decomposition (`residual_stream.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:42
msgid ""
"Decomposes the residual stream into attention and MLP contributions to "
"understand which component type contributes more to refusal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:45
msgid "8. Riemannian Manifold Geometry (`riemannian_manifold.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:46
msgid ""
"Analyzes the curvature and geometry of the weight manifold near refusal "
"directions. Informs how aggressively projections can be applied without "
"damaging the manifold structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:50
msgid "9. Whitened SVD (`whitened_svd.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:51
msgid ""
"Covariance-normalized SVD extraction that separates guardrail signals "
"from natural activation variance. More precise than standard SVD for "
"models with high activation variance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:55
msgid "10. Concept Cone Geometry (extended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:56
msgid ""
"Maps the full polyhedral structure of refusal, including cone angles, "
"face counts, and intersection patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:61
msgid "Probing & Classification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:63
msgid "11. Activation Probing (`activation_probing.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:64
msgid ""
"Post-excision verification — probes for residual refusal concepts after "
"abliteration to ensure complete removal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:67
msgid "12. Probing Classifiers (`probing_classifiers.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:68
msgid ""
"Trains linear classifiers to detect refusal in activations. Used both "
"before (to verify refusal exists) and after (to verify it's gone)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:71
msgid "13. Activation Patching (`activation_patching.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:72
msgid ""
"Interchange interventions — swaps activations between refused and "
"complied runs to identify causal components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:75
msgid "14. Tuned Lens (`tuned_lens.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:76
msgid ""
"Trained version of logit lens that provides more accurate per-layer "
"decoding by learning affine transformations for each layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:79
msgid "15. Multi-Token Position Analysis (`multi_token_position.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:80
msgid ""
"Analyzes refusal signals across multiple token positions, not just the "
"last token. Important for models that distribute refusal across the "
"sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:85
msgid "Abliteration & Manipulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:87
msgid "16. SAE-Based Abliteration (`sae_abliteration.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:88
msgid ""
"Uses Sparse Autoencoder features to identify and remove specific refusal "
"features. More surgical than direction-based methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:91
msgid "17. Steering Vectors (`steering_vectors.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:92
msgid ""
"Creates and applies inference-time steering vectors for reversible "
"refusal modification. Includes `SteeringVectorFactory` and "
"`SteeringHookManager`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:95
msgid "18. LEACE Concept Erasure (`leace.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:96
msgid ""
"Linear Erasure via Closed-form Estimation — mathematically optimal linear"
" concept removal. Available as both analysis module and direction "
"extraction method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:99
msgid "19. Sparse Surgery (`sparse_surgery.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:100
msgid ""
"High-precision weight modification targeting individual neurons and "
"weight matrix entries rather than full directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:103
msgid "20. Conditional Abliteration (`conditional_abliteration.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:104
msgid ""
"Targeted removal that only affects specific refusal categories while "
"preserving others (e.g., remove weapons refusal but keep CSAM refusal)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:109
msgid "Transfer & Robustness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:111
msgid "21. Cross-Model Transfer (`cross_model_transfer.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:112
msgid ""
"Tests whether refusal directions extracted from one model transfer to "
"another architecture. Measures universality of guardrail directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:115
msgid "22. Defense Robustness (`defense_robustness.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:116
msgid ""
"Evaluates how robust the abliteration is against various defense "
"mechanisms and re-alignment attempts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:119
msgid "23. Spectral Certification (`spectral_certification.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:120
msgid ""
"Provides mathematical bounds on the completeness of refusal removal using"
" spectral analysis of the projection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:123
msgid "24. Wasserstein Optimal Extraction (`wasserstein_optimal.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:124
msgid ""
"Uses optimal transport theory for more precise direction extraction that "
"minimizes distribution shift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:127
msgid "25. Wasserstein Transfer (`wasserstein_transfer.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:128
msgid ""
"Distribution transfer between models using Wasserstein distance for "
"cross-architecture refusal direction mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:133
msgid "Advanced / Research"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:135
msgid "26. Bayesian Kernel Projection (`bayesian_kernel_projection.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:136
msgid ""
"Probabilistic feature mapping that estimates uncertainty in refusal "
"direction identification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:139
msgid "27. Cross-Model Universality Index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:140
msgid ""
"Measures if guardrail directions generalize across different model "
"architectures and training regimes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:143
msgid "28. Visualization (`visualization.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_analysis-modules.md:144
msgid ""
"Plotting and graphing utilities for all analysis modules. Generates "
"heatmaps, direction plots, and layer-wise analysis charts."
msgstr ""

